<title>SAN MARINO: SOCCER-NETHERLANDS BEAT SAN MARINO 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-NETHERLANDS BEAT SAN MARINO 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MARINO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands beat San</p>
<p>Marino 6-0 (halftime 1-0) in their World Cup Group seven</p>
<p>qualifier on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:Dennis Bergkamp 40, 90, Aron Winter 63, Pierre van</p>
<p>Hooijdonk 70, Frank de Boer 74, John Bosman 85</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>San Marino: 1-Federico Gasperoni, 2-Mauro Valentini,</p>
<p>3-Damiano Vannucci, 4-Luca Gobbi, 5-William Guerra, 6-Matteoni,</p>
<p>7-Bryan Gasperoni (13-Leone Gasperoni 78), 8-Marco Mazza,</p>
<p>9-Paolo Montagna (18-Simone Bianchi 50), 10-Fabio Francini,</p>
<p>11-Riccardo Muccioli.</p>
<p>Netherlands: 1-Edwin van der Sar, 2-Aron Winter (12-Michael</p>
<p>Reiziger 73), 3-Jaap Stam, 4-Frank de Boer, 5-Arthur Numan,</p>
<p>6-Wim Jonk, 7-Pierre van Hooijdonk, 8-Ronald de Boer (17-John</p>
<p>Bosman 65), 9-Dennis Bergkamp, 10-Clarence Seedorf, 11-Boudewijn</p>
<p>Zenden.</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,800</p>
<p>    Standings     P   W   D   L  F    A  PTS</p>
<p> Netherlands	6   5   0   1  23   3  15</p>
<p> Belgium	    5   4   0   1  10   6  12</p>
<p> Turkey	     5   2   1   2  10   5   7</p>
<p> Wales		6   2   1   3  14  12   7</p>
<p> San Marino	 6   0   0   6   0  31   0</p>
